                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1 \to N
              factoring the morphisms from
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_325.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔉
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_326.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_327.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \to N
              uniquely factors through
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_328.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu : X_1 \to M_1
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_329.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_330.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ν
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_1 \longrightarrow^{\nu} M_1 \to N \to M_1
            %p
              where the last morphism is the inclusion of
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_331.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_332.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_333.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              imply that the morphism
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_334.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1 \to M_1
              in the above diagram is the identity, contradicting the non-surjectivity of
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_335.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \to M_1
              and thus the non-surjectivity of
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_336.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \to M_1
            %p
              Hence
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_337.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \to M_1
              is surjective. We also have that the smooth functions on
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_338.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              factor through
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_339.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_340.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              and
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_341.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1
              are isomorphic, but is enough to prove that the Hausdorffification of
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_342.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              is isomorphic to
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_343.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1
              (note that
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_344.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_345.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              induces an injective map from the underlying set of the Hausdorffification of
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_346.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              to the underlying set of
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_347.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_348.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
              be distinct points in the Hausdorffification of
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_349.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_350.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              which distinguishes them. As this smooth function factors through
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_351.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_352.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu(x) \ne \nu(y)
              and hence
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_353.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              is injective on the required underlying sets.
            %p
              Thus the inclusion functor
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_354.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M} \to \mathcal{H}
              preserves colimits.
          %p
            The inclusion of the category of Manifolds in that of all Frölicher spaces preserves limits (by the same proof as above) but not colimits. However, it is thus only the issue of being Hausdorff that prevents it preserving colimits. The simplest example is the classic non-Hausdorff manifold: consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequaliser
            of
            %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_355.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ﹨
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \smallsetminus \{0\}
            included in each piece of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_356.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \coprod \mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} Manifolds
            is simply
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_357.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_358.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0\}
          .query
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike
              \: What if we re-define “manifold” to remove the Hausdorff axiom? Does the inclusion into Frölicher spaces then preserve colimits?
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Stacey"}> Andrew
              \: I think so, but the inclusion from manifolds to Frölicher spaces is then not full. Let
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_359.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be the real line with a double point at the origin. Take a curve
              %math#mathml_8119de379c6e6a449dcec44a9d2398d1232435eb_360.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \to X
              which oscillates between the two points. This is a morphism into the Frölicher space, but not into the manifold.
            %p I think that to make it work, you have to redefine “Euclidean space” to include anything that becomes a Euclidean space upon Hausdorffification.
